# Repos the encoder suite needs checked out BESIDE it on the CI venue.
#
# Declaring a sibling here is what makes its cross-repo guards actually run. An
# UNdeclared sibling is not a neutral omission: every guard written against it
# resolves with existsSync, calls this.skip(), and the gate still prints PASS,
# so the run reports green having exercised none of them. Measured 2026-08-12,
# that gap was 3 guards (a venue carrying only hub + documentation ran 581
# passing / 6 pending where a full local checkout runs 584 / 3). See
# test/unit/sibling-coverage.test.js, which reports the surface this file leaves
# uncovered; the same gap applies to a sibling that is declared but missing.
#
# ci-dispatch.sh ships each of these at its canonical origin head (falling back
# to local HEAD) and REFUSES the push if one is not a checkout beside this repo.
# It also removes any leftover at the venue: on a shared venue that keeps a
# persistent checkout per repo, an undeclared sibling is not absent at all, it
# is whatever revision another repo's run left behind, and the guard silently
# compares against that.

# Vendored coins-registry byte-identity: BTC/LTC/DOGE/index/consensus_pin.
xchain-hub
# Action-manifest conformance, taproot-envelope golden vectors, and the
# compression-parameter reference.
xchain-documentation
# The envelope-recognition gate against the authoritative decoder.
xchain-decoder
# Compression-parameter twin parity.
xchain-sdk
# The inbound UTXO-record contract, the one seam carrying records INTO the
# encoder rather than out of it.
xchain-utxo-tracker
